WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.560
It's December 23rd.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.450
It's two days before Christmas,

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.010
and my wife has abandoned me.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.110
I'm trapped in mall traffic, sitting

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.850
behind the wheel and in the backseat

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.340
of my car Are truly two of the

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.170
most despicable and annoying human

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.910
beings I have ever met in my life.

00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:18.255
My children, Clara is six and

00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:19.785
Charlie is three, and there are

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:20.985
people in the world who will tell

00:00:20.985 --> 00:00:22.785
you, these kids are brilliant beams

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:24.255
of light, but that is bullshit

00:00:24.494 --> 00:00:26.145
because they are just like my wife.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:28.185
They are spending their entire lives

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:30.525
trying to slow me down and prevent me

00:00:30.525 --> 00:00:32.595
from doing the things that I want to do.

00:00:33.255 --> 00:00:34.800
These are children who literally.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.570
Stop and smell the roses.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.670
My wife takes them to flower shows

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.040
because they ask to go to flower shows.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.590
They stop me in parking lots and say,

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.690
look, dad, and point to the clouds and

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.640
say that cloud looks like a teapot.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.690
Take a picture.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.269
And I think I just wanna get in the store.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.310
And they talk to everyone.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.750
They talk to random

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.310
strangers all the time.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.040
They are dangerously friendly children.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.435
And my wife, my.

00:01:00.965 --> 00:01:03.575
My wife loves babies and she's given this

00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:05.315
to my daughter, so everywhere we go, my

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:07.655
daughter stops mothers with infants, and

00:01:07.655 --> 00:01:09.365
she has conversations with them like,

00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:11.675
what's the name of your baby, and how old

00:01:11.675 --> 00:01:13.805
is the baby and breast or bottle feeding?

00:01:13.805 --> 00:01:16.625
She's six years old and she's

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:18.455
just talking to everyone.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.700
And I'm sick of it.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.410
And on this day it is the worst day to

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.509
slow me down 'cause it's December 23rd.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.100
I have to buy Christmas presents 'cause

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.600
I haven't bought a single present.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.700
And I am beyond the Amazon Prime.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.170
Click and save your ass date.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.420
So I actually have to go into a

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.340
physical store and look at shit

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.500
on shelves to determine which ship

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.270
belongs to which person and what

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.740
will look good in wrapping paper.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.540
And I'm angry this day

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.650
is going bad for me.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.360
And my wife had the nerve on

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.460
this day to get a haircut.

00:01:47.825 --> 00:01:49.055
And when she goes to get a

00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:51.755
haircut, it is a three hour ordeal.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.665
She is a woman with short black hair.

00:01:54.665 --> 00:01:56.255
All she gets is a trim.

00:01:56.435 --> 00:01:58.115
The trim iest of trims, a trim I

00:01:58.115 --> 00:01:59.645
don't even notice most of the time,

00:01:59.795 --> 00:02:02.255
but it takes three hours because she

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.085
begins the process with someone who

00:02:04.085 --> 00:02:06.395
says, what are your goals for today?

00:02:06.785 --> 00:02:08.165
That is shit that I cannot.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.840
Abide bye.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.110
And so we're going to the mall, but

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.280
we can't go to the mall 'cause my

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.690
kids are hungry and we have to be

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.610
outside because like my wife, no one

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.320
wants to ever be in the house but me.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.270
I make enormous mortgage payments for a

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.250
home Nobody wants to spend a moment in.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.135
So we go to Panera.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.890
And when we go into Panera, I know

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.570
right away they've screwed up the floor.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.640
'cause they have the brown tiles

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.350
except in an occasional red tile.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.490
And if you have kids, you know that

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.570
that means your kids are just gonna

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.760
leap from one red tile to the other

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.500
and they're gonna knock people over

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.630
and land grilled cheese on the ground.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.130
So I say, go to the dining

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.420
room and find a booth.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.740
And I know they're gonna kill each other

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.420
while fighting over it, but I don't care

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.860
because they're not with me right now.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.290
So I go to the cashier and she's new.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.490
I can tell 'cause she's nervous

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.600
and so now I'm nervous and I

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.890
start giving her the order.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.450
And I say, listen, my daughter

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.350
is allergic to peanuts.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.850
Can you please note it on the order?

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.619
And she looks and she says, well, you

00:03:01.619 --> 00:03:03.059
didn't order anything with peanuts.

00:03:03.059 --> 00:03:03.809
And I'm like, ah.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:05.160
I say, I know, but could you

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.869
just note it because she's

00:03:06.869 --> 00:03:08.130
allergic and it's a good idea?

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.209
And she says, well, you really

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:10.829
didn't order anything with peanuts.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.880
And what I wanna say

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.869
to her is, listen lady.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.400
There's a substance in this world

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.870
that's basically in every food,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.250
as far as I can tell, that will

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.140
kill my daughter if she eats it.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.910
So could you please just fucking

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.710
put peanuts on the order?

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:23.700
But I don't do that because

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.990
I'm a better person than that.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.940
So I charge past her.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.230
I go past the counter and

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.640
into the employee area.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.620
I take two steps into the kitchen

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.240
and I go, listen, I, you're

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.560
gonna make a grilled cheese.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.670
And when you do, and then the

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.395
manager's right in front of me.

00:03:37.095 --> 00:03:38.385
And she says, sir, and I say,

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:39.825
no, you don't understand.

00:03:39.825 --> 00:03:40.725
Your cashier will not

00:03:40.725 --> 00:03:42.075
put peanuts on the order.

00:03:42.075 --> 00:03:43.215
And my daughter's allergic

00:03:43.245 --> 00:03:44.625
and she's not gonna die today.

00:03:44.625 --> 00:03:46.875
And the manager to her Everlasting credit

00:03:47.325 --> 00:03:50.715
softens, and she says, sir, I understand

00:03:50.775 --> 00:03:52.095
and I will take care of it, but you

00:03:52.095 --> 00:03:54.285
need to get out of my kitchen right now.

00:03:54.615 --> 00:03:55.305
And she's right.

00:03:55.305 --> 00:03:56.115
I'm crazy.

00:03:56.115 --> 00:03:57.525
And the kids have made me crazy.

00:03:57.735 --> 00:03:59.085
My wife has made me crazy.

00:03:59.415 --> 00:04:00.615
I get outta the kitchen,

00:04:01.335 --> 00:04:02.475
she finishes my order.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.035
I go to the dining room to find my

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:06.045
kids, and I cannot believe what I see.

00:04:06.405 --> 00:04:07.935
They have chosen a booth in the back.

00:04:07.935 --> 00:04:09.945
Clara is on one side, Charlie is on the

00:04:09.945 --> 00:04:12.915
